============================================================================
3. the density consequence (proved)
============================================================================
  alpha = log_rho 2 is IRRATIONAL: rho^a = 2^b forces
  81^a = 2^{b+6a}, i.e. 3^{4a} = 2^{b+6a}, so a = b = 0.
  Hence 5 alpha is irrational too, so the sampled phases
    phi_t = frac(5 alpha t - log_rho L)
  are equidistributed mod 1 by Weyl's theorem, for ANY L.
  On a surviving orbit C_t = 0 forces W_{5t} to receive exactly
  two visits (three would produce a counted start), and two visits
  happen exactly when phi_t lies in an arc of length
    delta = 3 - alpha = 0.0575254038.
  Equidistribution therefore gives
    upper density of {t : C_t = 0} <= delta = 5.752540%.
    sampled frequency at L = 1.0      : 0.05751  (delta = 0.05753)
    sampled frequency at L = 3.7      : 0.05751  (delta = 0.05753)
    sampled frequency at L = 1234.5   : 0.05753  (delta = 0.05753)
  so the 5t-sampled rotation does equidistribute, and the bound is
  not an artefact of the sampling.

  OBSERVED, from yesterday's census over t = 3..48:
    C_t = 0 at 39 of 46 scales = 84.8%, against the <= 5.753%
    that a surviving orbit would force: a factor 14.7 apart.

============================================================================
4. the reduction to an average bound
============================================================================
  C_t is a nonnegative integer, so
    #{t <= T : C_t >= 1} <= sum_{t<=T} C_t,
  hence density of zeros >= 1 - (1/T) sum C_t.  Combining with
  part 3, a surviving orbit needs
    1 - (1/T) sum_{t<=T} C_t <= delta   for all large T,
  i.e. (1/T) sum C_t >= 1 - delta = alpha - 2 = 0.9424745962.
  So it SUFFICES to prove
    liminf_T (1/T) sum_{t<=T} C_t < 0.9424746.

  where the observed data sits:
  quantity                           value        versus 0.9424746
  (1/T) sum C_t, T = 3..48           0.152174     BELOW by 6.2x
  (1/T) sum unres_t (trivial bound)  0.891304     BELOW by 5.7%
  heuristic mean of C_t              0.248590     BELOW by 3.8x
  heuristic mean of unres_t          1.000000     ABOVE by 6.1%

  THE DECISIVE POINT.  C_t <= unres_t always, and the expected
  value of unres_t is EXACTLY 1, because the window length 2^{5t}
  times the start density 2^t/64^t = 2^{-5t} is 1.  So the trivial
  bound (1/T) sum unres_t converges to 1, which EXCEEDS the
  threshold 0.9424746 by about 6 percent.
  Its observed value 0.8913 is below the threshold only by
  fluctuation at these scales.  Any proof must therefore use the
  three-visit restriction itself -- the factor
    2/rho^2 - 1 = 0.248590
  of the window -- and not merely the window count.
  Equivalently: an averaged discrepancy bound for the residues
  {r_w} in the bottom 24.86%% of W_{5t}, good to within a factor
  3.8 of the truth, suffices.  Nothing weaker than that will do,
  and nothing stronger is needed.

